    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d118">

                <pb facs="0236" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.60d2/4</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Pearson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 157</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-26">March 26, 1930</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department refers to the Legation’s
                    despatch No. 1537 of December 18, 1929, and desires to inform you that the
                    Department has received, from the Finnish Legation in Washington, the comments
                    of the Finnish Government with respect to the draft of the Treaty of Friendship,
                    Commerce and Consular Rights proposed to the Finnish Government on August 15,
                        1923.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d118-f1"/> The proposals of the Finnish
                    Government are under consideration by the Department, and it is contemplated
                    that a discussion of these proposals with the Finnish Minister in Washington
                    will be initiated in the near future.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Acting Secretary of State:<lb/><signed>G. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">Howland Shaw</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
